{#- Older absorbed scenes recalled by keyword match. Selection happens in code
    (context.archive._archive_entries); this template receives the matches.

    The "already happened" framing is load-bearing, not decoration: an
    unlabelled summary of an old scene reads as the current situation, and the
    model will play it as one. Vars: archive_entries ([{id, date, text}],
    newest first). -#}
{%- set lines = [] -%}
{%- for e in archive_entries -%}
{%- set _ = lines.append("- " ~ (("**" ~ e.date ~ "** — ") if e.date else "") ~ e.text) -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if lines %}# Earlier scenes
Recalled because this conversation touched on them. These scenes have already happened — they are history, not the current moment.

{{ lines | join("\n") }}{% endif -%}
